delphi-ticket-prediction microservice SCPs the AlarmMonitor log files generated by delphi-alarm-monitoring  microservice for ```every``` 20 minutes and fetches prepare*NotifyRequest logs from the AlarmMonitor log files, compares the alarmcode from the prepare*NotifyRequest logs with the Category CFG file, if there are fault alarms present like inact, and also it check for the occurrences of alarms, i.e. if it is INACT then apply 1st rule, if the BHR occurrences is 2 then apply the next rule, this way, it will apply prediction rules and if a prediction rule is satisfied, then immediately it will prepare test required, it will check all the rules one by one and if Test required per ONT means (that particular Device is eligible for prediction/testing or not), it will prepare DELPHI request and send to DTE for testing, DTE performs DIAGNOSTIC tests , and apply smart fixes if applicable and sends acknowledgement to ticket prediction, then ticket prediction will create a ticket and dispatches technician